  "title": "Two ant colonies meeting at a border",
  "question": "Does this read as two colonies holding a line against each other, rather than one crowd of ants? And does the way they meet feel like rivalry, or just like traffic?",
  "context_md": "Round 35 lane D. Yellow is one colony, blue is the other -- they were founded 58 cells apart and have walked into each other. 4,000 frames, one seed, 24 ants per colony.\n\n**The counts for this exact run:** 31 encounters where an ant stood in reach of a stranger, of which **8 became a bite and 23 ended in a display and a step back** -- escalation 0.26. 6 kills. Before tonight's change every one of those 31 would have been a bite, because an encounter and a fight were the same event.\n\nWhat I am asking about is only what is on screen: whether two colours meeting in the middle of a bed reads as two colonies, and whether it has the feel of a border. The numbers above are not the question.",
